			<div class="content" id="post-content-4855801">
									

<p>While I do like the core concept you're going for, the SCP itself feels like a deviation of a <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foster%27s_Home_for_Imaginary_Friends">particular cartoon</a>. While that's not necessarily a bad thing, you DID put your own spin on it after all, but for me, I think it's a bit way too similar to said cartoon to the point readers might just see this as a rip-off, or that it's lacking originality.</p>
<p>What does catch my attention is how you're trying to show the more sympathetic and kind side of the Foundation, so I suggest you keep that story intact if you decide to refine the SCP. If I were to come up with this concept, it would be that the &quot;imaginary friends&quot; are actually interdimensional parasites that only feed on children.</p>
<p>Moving on, your English might need some improvement if you're gonna try to write in a clinical tone. I'm not saying you're barely understandable, your English is good enough for normal conversations and you did explain your concept well, but a little bit of studying and improvement can never hurt and will only make your writing even better.</p>

							</div>

								
					
