														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4855792">
									

<p>Hello, fellow members. I am a freelance horror writer currently going to school at Full Sail U for creative writing. I was always a fan of the SCP genre of things, since long before I started writing. You could say, among other things, it somewhat inspired me to my own writing. And now that I am confident enough in my particular form of horror, I have decided to present myself among you all and begin the process of adding my own work to this glorious work of art we know as the SCP Foundation.</p>
<p>Personally, I have a deep and longing fascination with the horrors of the mind. This sprouted from an experiment I performed on myself with lucidity and the effects of uncontrolled experimentation. You see, the lucid state in which I brought upon myself didn't exactly stop when I wanted it to. It became abundantly clear to me that no matter what I did, I would eventually be conscious when I went to sleep. In this time spent in a lucid state, I began to feel as if I was being followed by something I had not created there. Or perhaps someone I had created unknowingly. Eventually, the method I had used to gain lucidity wore and with it, the state.</p>
<p>Nevertheless, I lay awake at night knowing that he&#8230; or it&#8230; is still in there somewhere.</p>
<p>Sorry if that was a little too much.</p>

