<p>I'm,,,somewhat conflicted on this. The Elevator Pitch introduces a lot of intriguing elements, particularly around it actively consuming information; but my concern is that the actual narrative here feels&#8230;like it doesn't really go anywhere interesting.</p>
<p>Really, I'm just kinda looking at the various writing elements you're using (the experiment logs, the mtf explorations, the interviews, the failed neutralisation etc etc) and feeling like there's a lot of stuff going on that doesn't really collapse into feeling like it's telling one coherent story so much as just like, throwing in a lot of elements in an attempt to see what parts stick.</p>
<p>This kinda feels like it touches on a lot of parts of site lore ('Pataphysics via the authors coming in, antimemetics from the behaviour of the scp, pattern screamers via the black voids it leaves behind) without really doing anything new with the elements beyond just kinda mentioning them; and I'm not sure how much of this is an issue per se except in that you don't really do a lot narratively with this.</p>

