<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights</strong>: Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type</strong>: SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre</strong>: Other? Big Potential threat but not an absolutely terrifying being. I don’t know how to clarify. Government takeover scary and not Monster scary</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch</strong>: A child humanoid SCP that possesses anomalous abilities similar to a comic character. Including high levels of strength, agility, along with being able to fire beams from his hand that when observed up close are similar in nature to the state of matter plasma. The SCP claims to be a Hero of justice from another world and has vowed to fight for the safety of this planet. The SCP is aware of every law pertaining to each individual stat and country from sources it refuses to foretell.</p>
<p>Central Narrative: A basic exploration of the idea of if Superman had zero guidance or experience with handling situations becoming who he is. And if it’s relatively agreed that the event would be catastrophic how so? (I swear to God I am not copying off of the kid that can open portals to items he wants. I promise it’s different and good.)</p>
<p>Hook/Attention-Grabber: Most SCP usually have a proper handle on how they work by the time they are in the foundation. The SCP has no idea how to use its anomaly for its said purpose. It is not familiar at all with standard procedure pursuing law breaking or threats of any kind. For example the SCP will attempt to destroy any person breaking these laws and anything in the way of its pursuit. It also has refused to negotiate on any other method of dealing with said criminals with any local authority. The SCP also seems to behave like a child</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes</strong>: The child was sited from a wormhole that opened near the asteroid belt and closed into earth crashing in a forest close enough to the foundation for recovery with minimal complications.</p>

