			<div class="content" id="post-content-4855546">
									

<p>Looking for feedback on idea : A SCP with extraordinary rhetorical skills and a fascinating bowler hat.</p>
<p><em>I moved and trimmed your thread summary, since it was taking up extra space in the main forum screen. Try to keep thread descriptions (the text in the little box under the thread title) and titles short so you don't crowd out other authors in the forum listing. ~Zyn</em></p>
<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Horror, Intrigue</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Don't know yet</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A man arrives at SCP site XXX by foot, wearing a black coat and a black bowler hat on his head. Guards outside the gates are astonished, they didn't see him coming down the road. The man asks to speak with Director XXXX about something he does not wish to share with personel under level 4 clearance. The guards are surprised ; this man knows the jargon of the Foundation, but who is he? He does not seem to be wearing any badge or signet from any governmental or private corporation. The guards would have normaly turn down any such request coming from a civilian, but something about this man seems peculiar.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The man is a malignous entity that relies on speech and rhetorical skills to trap humans into mind-wrecking revelations about their lives. He says he has ultimate knowledge on things in the universe, but before answering any questions, the man says he will only answer if he is allowed to ask a question after his answer.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Eventually, the man tries to find a way to get access to SCP-343, pretending he has old business to take care of with &quot;what the foundation call SCP-343&quot;. He also asks to meet all the single SCP kept in this facility. This request is denied, but he seems to already know which SCPs are located into the facility. -(Here I will be provinding discussion log demonstrating the man's ability to use rhetoric and revealing undisclosed information about the foundation. This will serve the idea that he is all-knowing, but takes pleasure in playing with weak minds.)</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> This SCP is somewhere between the Keter/Thaumiel class. The man agrees to containement because he let's the foundation keep him : &quot;You and your foundation are only able to contain me because I allow it. Keep asking me questions and I will glady be contained&quot;. He does not seem physicaly dangerous, but he is highly dangerous when questions asked to him are poorly developped. Although, if the questions are well developped, then they can reveal extraordinary knowledge about certain SCPs and anomalies. The knowledge of this man is beyond human intelligence. Many researchers try to have &quot;mind&quot; fights with him but they all end up being beaten (and some have their mind's destroyed). I believe the hook would be that the more discussion the foundation researchers have with this man, the more they start believe he is in fact the devil -(I will add theological references and such).</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I would like to get your feedback on this idea and also if you think this is interesting enough to have as a SCP. I really enjoy SCPs that are trickters and that don't seem to be dangerous at first. Feel free to ask questions, I really want to make it as clear as possible! Thanks :)<br /></p>
